{#- VRishi block library v1.1 — PSR-aligned. Original wording throughout.
    p=profile ctx, s=session plan.
    <mark name="await_*"/> = ideomotor checkpoint (live: practitioner waits for nod;
    XR/auto: gesture-detect or fixed pause). <mark name="cue_snap"/> = snap/audio cue slot. -#}
{%- macro brk(t) -%}<break time="{{ t }}"/>{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro await(name) -%}<mark name="await_{{ name }}"/>{{ brk('4s') }}{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro snap() -%}<mark name="cue_snap"/>{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro deep_sleep(level='strong') -%}{{ snap() }}<emphasis level="{{ level }}">Deep sleep.</emphasis>{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro phs_short(p) -%}
<p>And from now on, whenever we are working together for the purpose of hypnosis, and with your permission, the words <emphasis level="strong">deep sleep</emphasis> bring you back to this state quickly, calmly, and deeply, and the body relaxes. {{ brk('1200ms') }}</p>
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro pre_talk(p, s) -%}
<mark name="stage_pre_talk"/>
{#- YES-SET: 3 pacing truisms → 1 lead connector → suggestion (NLP 1 p.12: match→pace→lead) -#}
<p>You made it here today. {{ brk('400ms') }}You are sitting in that chair. {{ brk('400ms') }}You can hear the sound of my voice clearly. {{ brk('500ms') }}And that means the part of you that wants this change is already at work. {{ brk('700ms') }}</p>
<p>So before we begin, here is what hypnosis actually is. {{ brk('500ms') }}
It is a natural state — you drift in and out of it every day, in movies, in daydreams, on familiar drives. {{ brk('600ms') }}
It is a narrow, comfortable focus that lets the protective filter of the mind relax, so a negative pattern can be exchanged for a positive one. {{ brk('700ms') }}
When I say the words deep sleep, that is a cue for this relaxed state — not actual sleep. {{ brk('500ms') }}
You stay aware the whole time, you hear everything, you cannot get stuck, and you would never do or say anything you wouldn't do wide awake. It is not a truth serum. {{ brk('800ms') }}
{#- MILTON MODEL: indirect suggestion + presupposition -#}
If your mind wanders, that is normal — it will return to my voice on its own. {{ brk('600ms') }}
Some people find that they feel light and tingly, some feel pleasantly heavy, some simply feel calm. Whatever you experience is right for you. {{ brk('700ms') }}
And you may begin to wonder whether you are hypnotized — that wondering is usually the sign that you are.</p>
{#- PACING current experience → LEADING to participation -#}
<p>This is a do-with process, not a do-to process — your participation and imagination are the engine. {{ brk('600ms') }}
The reason you are here is {{ s.presenting_issue }}, and as you begin to work with the subconscious directly, the change you have been forcing becomes far easier. {{ brk('700ms') }}
I will run a few tests today to learn how your mind takes in information. You cannot pass or fail them — so no helping, no hindering — they simply tell me how to work in your exact style. {{ brk('600ms') }}
Any questions before we start? {{ await('questions') }}
{#- PRESUPPOSITION: assumes the goal is already in motion -#}
Good — and because of that, today we begin building the new associations that carry you to your goal.</p>
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro theory_of_mind(p, s) -%}
<mark name="stage_tom"/>
{#- LEAD from pre-talk agreement → new information. PRESUPPOSITION: "why this works" -#}
<p>Let me show you how the mind is organized, because it explains exactly why this works. {{ brk('600ms') }}
At the base sits the primitive area — pure survival instinct — with two settings: fight, which pushes through stress, and flight, the urge to withdraw and escape it. {{ brk('800ms') }}
{#- PACING: truism about childhood → lead to subconscious -#}
From birth to about age eight, the mind accepts nearly everything as true. That is when the programming forms — some of it positive, some negative — and those experiences become the known associations: what we believe, what feels familiar. {{ brk('900ms') }}
Those associations make up the subconscious mind — about eighty-eight percent of your mental power. {{ brk('700ms') }}
As we grow, a filter forms above it — the critical mind — whose whole job is to protect the known, even when the known is the problem. {{ brk('700ms') }}
And on top, the conscious mind: logic, reasoning, decisions, willpower — the willpower that never quite works when you need it — only about twelve percent of the power.</p>
{#- REFRAME: presenting_issue as mechanical, not personal failure -#}
<p>So here is what has been happening with {{ s.presenting_issue }}. {{ brk('500ms') }}
The decision to change starts in the conscious mind, travels down, hits the critical filter, and gets checked against the old programming. {{ brk('600ms') }}
The programming resists, the filter blocks the change, and the same pattern runs again — {{ s.critical_mind.why }} {{ brk('800ms') }}
{#- MILTON: indirect certainty + EMBEDDED COMMAND: "accept this" -#}
And you might notice how that pattern has been running on its own, without your permission. {{ brk('600ms') }}
Hypnosis takes that same intention and moves it past the filter, straight to the subconscious, where we install the new pattern with positive suggestion: {{ s.critical_mind.how }} {{ brk('700ms') }}
I will work with the eighty-eight percent. You work with the twelve. Together, that is one hundred percent. {{ brk('600ms') }}
{#- TAG QUESTION: yes-anchor (NLP 1 p.12: rapport via agreement) -#}
That makes sense, doesn't it? {{ await('tom_yes') }}
And the way we begin is by testing your suggestibility.</p>
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro suggestibility_questions(p) -%}
<mark name="stage_sugg_questions"/>
<p>Keep the eyes closed and just answer naturally. {{ brk('500ms') }}
Have you ever walked or talked in your sleep? {{ await('q1') }}
Have you ever woken in the night feeling unable to move or speak for a moment? {{ await('q2') }}
After an argument, do you replay what you could have said? {{ await('q3') }}
If you think of biting into a sour lemon, does your mouth water? {{ await('q4') }}
Can you picture things clearly in your mind? {{ await('q5') }}</p>
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro induction_arm_raising(p) -%}
<mark name="stage_induction"/>
<p>Sit upright, feet flat on the floor, and rest your {{ p.vars.get('induction_arm','left') }} arm on the table. {{ brk('600ms') }}
Look at that arm now, from the elbow to the fingertips — take a good picture of it — and close your eyes. {{ brk('900ms') }}
See that arm and hand in your mind, and when you can remember exactly what they look like, nod your head. {{ await('visualize_arm') }}</p>
{{ suggestibility_questions(p) }}
<mark name="stage_physio"/>
<p>Now, as you begin to enter hypnosis, your body will show a series of changes. I will notice them before you do — when you become aware of each one, just nod and let me know. {{ brk('800ms') }}
First, the breathing tends to grow deeper as the body takes in more oxygen. When you notice your breathing deepening, nod your head. {{ await('breath') }}
The lips, mouth, and throat may feel a little dry, with an urge to swallow. Completely natural — when you notice it, nod. {{ await('swallow') }}
And notice the eyes now — that faint fluttering of the eyes beneath the lids. {{ brk('700ms') }}
That is the first stage of hypnosis.</p>
<mark name="stage_conversion"/>
{% if p.mode == 'literal' -%}
{#- LITERAL/PHYSICAL mode: direct embedded commands, pacing physical sensations -#}
<p>Bring your attention to the elbow pressing into the table, down the forearm, into the wrist, the hand, the fingertips. {{ brk('700ms') }}
{#- PACING kinesthetic → LEADING to lightness -#}
You can feel where your hands are resting. {{ brk('400ms') }}And as that happens, that hand is becoming light. {{ brk('400ms') }}Very light. {{ brk('400ms') }}<emphasis level="strong">Lighter and lighter</emphasis> — light as a feather, and then lighter than that. {{ brk('800ms') }}
{#- DOUBLE BIND: both options lead to lifting (NLP 1/Erickson) -#}
And whether the lifting begins in the fingers first, or in the wrist, either way it rises. {{ brk('700ms') }}
Small pulling and jerking motions are starting in the hand. {{ brk('700ms') }}
{#- PACING opposite hand → compound suggestion -#}
At the same time, the other hand grows heavier against your leg, your feet press into the floor, your back rests against the chair. {{ brk('800ms') }}
The deeper you go, the more you notice — each breath makes the light hand lighter and the heavy hand heavier — when you feel that difference in weight, nod your head. {{ await('weight_diff') }}
The hand is lifting now — rising — pivoting at the elbow, the palm turning inward — lifting, rising, twisting, turning, upward and inward, the hand drawn to the face. {{ brk('700ms') }}
{#- POWER-WORD REPETITION (P3 workbook): message-unit overload drives physical conversion -#}
Lifting, rising, higher and higher, lighter and lighter, pulling up with every breath now. {{ brk('700ms') }}
Higher and higher, lighter and lighter — light as a feather — pulling, jerking, moving up, up, and up. {{ brk('900ms') }}
{#- HEAD-TO-HAND close (P3): head drops to meet the rising hand, closing the gap both ways; steer to brow, not eyes -#}
And the head grows heavy now, dropping gently down to meet that rising hand — the hand toward the brow, the brow toward the hand, closer and closer together. {{ brk('800ms') }}
With every inhale, the arm and hand go up — and on the exhale the head drops down to meet the hand — closer and closer together. {{ brk('1200ms') }}</p>
{%- else -%}
{#- INFERRED/EMOTIONAL mode: Milton model language, imagination-based -#}
<p>Let your attention drift to the elbow resting comfortably on the table, down through the forearm, into the wrist, the hand, the fingertips. {{ brk('700ms') }}
{#- MILTON MODEL: "you might imagine" + permissive framing -#}
And you might imagine that hand becoming lighter — as if many powerful helium balloons were tied around the wrist — light as a feather, and then even lighter. {{ brk('900ms') }}
{#- PRESUPPOSITION: "as you allow that" assumes compliance -#}
As you allow that, you may notice little pulling or tugging motions beginning — you are creating that sensation, and that gives you a greater sense of control. {{ brk('900ms') }}
{#- PACING: kinesthetic truth → lead to nod -#}
And at the same time you can feel the other hand a little heavier on your leg, the feet against the floor, the rhythm of your breath — and when you notice the light hand and the heavy hand feeling different, you can nod. {{ await('weight_diff') }}
{#- DOUBLE BIND: three options, all lead to hand-to-face -#}
And it becomes a floating feeling — a tendency to <emphasis level="strong">lift with each breath</emphasis> — rising now, pivoting, the palm turning gently inward — and I wonder whether it feels more like the hand being drawn to the face, or the face to the hand, or both drawn together. I will let you decide. {{ brk('1200ms') }}</p>
{%- endif %}
<p>And when the hand comes all the way in to touch the face — the moment you make skin contact — nod your head, and you will reach your peak of suggestibility and enter the hypnotic sleep. {{ await('skin_contact') }}
{{ deep_sleep() }} {{ brk('1500ms') }}</p>
{{ phs_short(p) }}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro count_5_0(p) -%}
<mark name="stage_count_5_0"/>
<p>Gently let the hand come back down to rest. {{ brk('800ms') }}
Now a count from five down to zero, and each count carries you deeper. {{ brk('700ms') }}
Five — going down now, deeper into hypnosis. {{ brk('800ms') }}
Four — the body releasing, relaxing, letting go. {{ brk('800ms') }}
Three — an emotional calmness. {{ brk('800ms') }}
Two — the mind relaxing now. {{ brk('800ms') }}
One — deeper and deeper. {{ brk('800ms') }}
And zero — {{ deep_sleep() }} {{ brk('1200ms') }}</p>
{{ phs_short(p) }}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro deepener_reactional(p) -%}
<mark name="stage_reactional"/>
<p>In a moment — not yet — I will ask you to open your eyes and fix them on a point above you, and when I say deep sleep, they close again and you go twice as deep. {{ brk('900ms') }}
Open your eyes. {{ brk('2s') }}And — {{ deep_sleep() }} Twice as deep. {{ brk('1200ms') }}
Open your eyes. {{ brk('2s') }}And — {{ deep_sleep() }} {{ brk('1200ms') }}
Open your eyes. {{ brk('2s') }}And — {{ deep_sleep() }} Twice as deep. {{ brk('1200ms') }}
One more time — open your eyes. {{ brk('2s') }}And — {{ deep_sleep() }} {{ brk('1500ms') }}</p>
{{ phs_short(p) }}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro deepener_heavy_light(p) -%}
<mark name="stage_heavy_light"/>
<p>Open your eyes and stretch both arms out in front of you at shoulder height. {{ brk('800ms') }}
One palm faces up. The other hand turns sideways, thumb pointing to the ceiling. {{ brk('700ms') }}
Close your eyes. {{ brk('600ms') }}
On the open palm I am placing a heavy book — feel its weight pressing that arm down. {{ brk('900ms') }}
And around the upright thumb I am tying many powerful helium balloons, pulling that arm upward. {{ brk('900ms') }}
One arm pressed down, the other drawn up — let the arms respond. {{ brk('3s') }}
Good. Release both ideas, let the arms float gently down to your lap — and {{ deep_sleep() }} {{ brk('1500ms') }}</p>
{{ phs_short(p) }}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro deepener(p) -%}
<mark name="stage_deepener"/>
{% set style = p.deepener_style %}
{% if style == 'slide' -%}
<p>Imagine the gentlest playground slide, with {{ p.count_from }} soft pillows waiting at the bottom. {{ brk('700ms') }}
{% for n in range(p.count_from, 0, -1) %}{{ n }} — sliding down, easy and safe. {{ brk('800ms') }}{% endfor %}
And you land in the pillows, twice as relaxed.</p>
{%- elif style == 'garden_path' -%}
<p>Picture a level garden path with {{ p.count_from }} smooth stepping stones, each one carrying you deeper into calm. {{ brk('800ms') }}
{% for n in range(p.count_from, 0, -1) %}{{ n }} — a soft, steady step, deeper down. {{ brk('900ms') }}{% endfor %}
At the last stone you settle onto a comfortable bench, twice as deep.</p>
{%- else -%}
{#- STAIRCASE: workbook p.20 — 20 steps, left/right alternation, "twice as deep" interspersions -#}
<p>Before you is a beautiful staircase, well-lit, with sturdy, smooth handrails, and it has {{ p.count_from }} steps leading down to a bottom landing. {{ brk('700ms') }}
With each step down you deepen your state of hypnosis and more deeply relax and let go. {{ brk('900ms') }}
{% for n in range(p.count_from, 0, -1) %}{% if n % 2 == 0 %}Left foot at {% else %}Right foot at {% endif %}{{ n }}{% if n % 5 == 2 %} — twice as deep{% elif n % 5 == 0 %} — letting go{% elif n % 3 == 0 %} — feeling yourself deeply relax{% endif %} — deeper down. {{ brk('900ms') }}
{% endfor %}
At the bottom — {{ deep_sleep('moderate') }}</p>
{%- endif %} {{ brk('1500ms') }}
{{ phs_short(p) }}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro eye_fascination(p) -%}
{#- Secondary induction / deepener. Lane by suggestibility mode:
    inferred/blended -> permissive (withhold closure, blur imagery, invite);
    literal          -> paternal-rapid (blink<->heavy loop, drive lids down,
                        cue_forehead touch on close + cue_limpness hands-drop).
    Source: Practicum Scripts 101-5 item 15 (permissive baseline) +
    classic paternal variant (forehead touch + limpness convincer). -#}
<mark name="stage_eye_fascination"/>
<p>Let the eyes come open for a moment, and pick a spot on the ceiling a little above your eye line — so the eyes look up just slightly to find it — and rest your gaze there. {{ brk('900ms') }}
Let the eyes settle on that one point, without moving them. {{ brk('1200ms') }}</p>
{% if p.mode != 'literal' -%}
{#- PERMISSIVE lane (E / blended): urge built by withholding closure; blur imagery convincer -#}
<p>As you keep looking at that spot — the gaze may drift and come back, gently, easily — you can begin to notice the small muscles around the eyes, {{ brk('400ms') }}how they hold the eyes up, {{ brk('400ms') }}and the eyelids, and what they feel like. {{ brk('900ms') }}
You may begin to blink a little more often {{ await('ef_blink') }}
That's it — and the breathing might deepen as you relax. {{ brk('800ms') }}
As the eyes rest on that spot, the mind wrapped around it, the eyelids may start to feel heavy, and the eyes may want to close. But not just yet — let them stay open a little longer. {{ brk('900ms') }}
And blinking a little more now {{ await('ef_blink2') }}
you might notice that blink is a little slower than normal. {{ brk('800ms') }}
Many people, entering hypnosis, find the focus going soft — the vision blurring — and as you look at that spot it might waver, or blur, or seem to shift shape or color. {{ brk('1000ms') }}That's it. {{ brk('700ms') }}
And you may notice the arms and legs growing heavy as the eyelids grow heavier and heavier, and how good it would feel to let those tired eyes simply relax and close. {{ brk('900ms') }}
As you focus on that spot and the eyes grow more tired, heavier, more fatigued — when you are ready, you can let them close. {{ await('ef_close') }}
And closing the eyes means you can relax now — it feels good, peaceful, as you really let yourself go. {{ brk('900ms') }}</p>
{%- else -%}
{#- PATERNAL-RAPID lane (P / literal): message-unit overload; blink<->heavy reciprocal loop;
    cue_forehead = light forehead touch on close; cue_limpness = lift-and-drop hands -#}
<p>Keep staring at that spot — don't take the eyes off it — and as you stare, the eyelids are already beginning to feel heavy, {{ brk('300ms') }}heavy and tired, the muscles around the eyes working, tiring, wanting to rest. {{ brk('600ms') }}
The longer you stare, the heavier they get — heavier and heavier — the eyes tiring, blinking {{ await('ef_blink') }}
that's it — and every blink makes them heavier, and the heavier they get the more they blink, and the more they blink the heavier they get. {{ brk('500ms') }}
So heavy now they want to close — <emphasis level="strong">let them get heavier</emphasis> — heavier — so heavy they are going to close, closing down now, heavier and heavier, closing, {{ brk('400ms') }}closing. {{ await('ef_close') }}</p>
<p><mark name="cue_forehead"/>{{ deep_sleep() }} {{ brk('1200ms') }}</p>
<p><mark name="cue_limpness"/>And the whole body going loose, {{ brk('300ms') }}limp, {{ brk('300ms') }}heavy — every muscle letting go, deeper with each breath. {{ brk('800ms') }}
That's it — loose and limp all over, deeply relaxed. {{ brk('900ms') }}</p>
{%- endif %}
<p>Breathe in for a moment {{ brk('700ms') }}and breathe out — and let that relaxation double through the whole body. {{ brk('900ms') }}
Deeper and deeper, all the way down. {{ brk('800ms') }}
Five — the body relaxing — four — the mind letting go — three — emotionally calm — two — one — zero — {% if p.mode == 'literal' %}{{ deep_sleep() }}{% else %}{{ deep_sleep('moderate') }}{% endif %} {{ brk('1200ms') }}</p>
{{ phs_short(p) }}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro auto_dual_induction(p) -%}
{#- Alternative PRIMARY induction (Practicum 101-5 item 8). Pulse-focus + repeat-after-me;
    self-spoken counts drive message-unit overload. Speed the count, speak slightly over them.
    Original wording. Marks: await_pulse (client finds pulse), then self-spoken descent. -#}
<mark name="stage_auto_dual"/>
<p>Sit up straight, feet flat on the floor. {{ brk('600ms') }}
Hold your {{ p.vars.get('induction_arm','left') }} arm out, and place the index finger of the other hand on that wrist — feel for your pulse. When you have it, nod. {{ await('pulse') }}
Good. Now stare directly at the fingernail of that index finger, and keep part of your attention on the pulse. {{ brk('700ms') }}
All your attention on that fingernail — take a slow, deep breath. {{ brk('800ms') }}
In a moment I will say some phrases, and you will say each one out loud, right after me. Everything I say, you say. Nod if that's clear. {{ await('repeat_ok') }}</p>
<p>Repeat after me. {{ brk('500ms') }}
I will now enter the state of hypnosis. {{ brk('1200ms') }}
For reasons of deep relaxation and self-control. {{ brk('1200ms') }}
I will count from five down to zero. {{ brk('1000ms') }}
And with each count I will become more deeply relaxed. {{ brk('1000ms') }}
When I reach zero, I will go deep asleep. {{ brk('1200ms') }}</p>
{#- Accelerate here: shorter pauses, slight overlap = message-unit overload -#}
<p>Five — my breathing growing deep, gentle, and rhythmic. {{ brk('700ms') }}
Four — a heaviness in my eyelids, drowsier and sleepier. {{ brk('700ms') }}
Three — every muscle, nerve, and fiber relaxing, deeply relaxing. {{ brk('600ms') }}
Two — my arms, my legs, my whole body now deeply relaxed. {{ brk('600ms') }}
One — my eyelids closing, the breathing rhythmic, deeply relaxed. {{ brk('600ms') }}
Zero — {{ deep_sleep() }} {{ brk('1500ms') }}</p>
{{ phs_short(p) }}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro guided_imagery(p) -%}
{#- Secondary induction (Practicum 101-5 item 17). Breath close → head-to-toe release →
    5-0 → meadow/tree/leaf/blade-of-grass journey with embedded perseverance/motivation frame.
    "can't visualize → imagine/conceptualize" fallback baked in. Original wording. -#}
<mark name="stage_guided_imagery"/>
<p>To begin, simply focus. Feel your breath. {{ brk('600ms') }}
An easy breath in through the nose, and slowly out through the mouth. {{ brk('800ms') }}
And in your own mind, give yourself permission to allow me to guide you on a pleasant journey. {{ brk('700ms') }}
On the exhale of your third or fourth breath, let your eyes close. {{ brk('1500ms') }}
Although not everyone visualizes, everyone can imagine — if you can't see it as a picture, that's alright; we'll use the other senses too, or simply think about it, or conceptualize. {{ brk('900ms') }}</p>
<p>Let's start at the top of the head, and gently work downward, allowing any pressure inside to release. {{ brk('600ms') }}
Down over the face, especially the jaw, releasing tension — a pleasant feeling you're allowing. {{ brk('600ms') }}
Flowing down over the shoulders, down the arms and hands, the pressures of the day releasing. {{ brk('600ms') }}
Down through the chest and the back, the stomach and lower back, {{ brk('500ms') }}through the hips, and all the way down the legs to the tips of the toes — a gentle letting go. {{ brk('900ms') }}
Now count backward in your own mind with me, from five down to zero — five, {{ brk('500ms') }}four, {{ brk('500ms') }}three, even deeper, {{ brk('500ms') }}two, {{ brk('500ms') }}one, {{ brk('500ms') }}and zero — {{ deep_sleep('moderate') }} {{ brk('1200ms') }}</p>
<p>Feel the rhythm of your breath, and let your imaginative mind open. {{ brk('700ms') }}
Imagine we're walking through a beautiful meadow on a wonderful day, the temperature just as you'd like it. {{ brk('700ms') }}
You feel the earth beneath your feet, a sweet smell of nature around you, perhaps wildflowers in bloom. {{ brk('700ms') }}
A beautiful bird crosses the sky — majestic and free — and a free feeling rises in you. {{ brk('700ms') }}
You hear a gentle breeze through distant trees. {{ brk('700ms') }}
Ahead, on a little hill beyond the meadow, stands a single, beautiful tree. {{ brk('600ms') }}
As you come closer you see how wonderfully it's formed, leaves moving in the breeze — the sounds and smells and images all easing you. {{ brk('800ms') }}
Near the top, on the tip of one branch, a single leaf. {{ brk('600ms') }}
You stop and watch it twist and turn, twist and turn — and something in you knows it's about to break free. {{ brk('700ms') }}
And all at once the leaf is free, the breeze carrying it slowly, gliding down, down toward the earth, to rest near the base of the tree. {{ brk('800ms') }}
You walk over and look down — the earth, the leaf, the roots of the tree — and there, a single blade of grass. {{ brk('700ms') }}
It has persevered and grown strong through its own motivation — the same way you are motivated in your life. {{ brk('800ms') }}
And you can take what we've talked about, begin to understand it, and help yourself with it — and that feels wonderful. {{ brk('900ms') }}
So in this beautiful place — the smells, the sounds, the positive feelings in body and mind — we carry all of it forward with you. {{ brk('1000ms') }}</p>
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro self_hypnosis_teach(p) -%}
{#- Homework teach-back (Practicum 101-5 item 18). Practitioner instructs the client on the
    take-home self-hypnosis protocol. Client is AWAKE for this (post-emergence coaching) —
    no deep_sleep/PHS here; it ends by confirming they have the steps. Original wording. -#}
<mark name="stage_self_hypnosis_teach"/>
<p>Before you go, let's set you up with a version you can do on your own, at home. {{ brk('600ms') }}
You'll use three keywords we'll choose together: a physical word, an emotional word, and the intellectual cue — deep sleep. Keep them simple and personal. {{ brk('900ms') }}
Nod when you have your physical word in mind. {{ await('sh_physical_word') }}
And your emotional word. {{ await('sh_emotional_word') }}</p>
<p>Here's the sequence. {{ brk('400ms') }}
Sit somewhere semi-comfortable, and create an eye fascination — fix your gaze on a point above and in front of you. {{ brk('700ms') }}
Take three slow breaths, in through the nose, out through the mouth, relaxing the jaw — and on the exhale of the third breath, let the eyes close. {{ brk('800ms') }}
Bring your attention to the top of the head, and silently repeat your physical keyword — then carry it down through every part of the body, section by section, flowing with that physical feeling. {{ brk('900ms') }}
Count yourself down from five to zero. At zero, rest on your breathing and repeat your emotional keyword — and really let yourself feel it. {{ brk('800ms') }}
Then walk down a staircase of twenty steps, and at the bottom say your intellectual cue to yourself: deep sleep. {{ brk('800ms') }}
Now give yourself the suggestions we've prepared — with feeling, meaning every word — and repeat them a few times. {{ brk('900ms') }}
When you're ready to return, count from zero up to five, and tell yourself: eyes open, wide awake. {{ brk('700ms') }}</p>
<p>Practice it once a day. Each repetition makes your own cue stronger and the change more automatic. {{ brk('500ms') }}
Nod if you have the steps. {{ await('sh_steps_ok') }}</p>
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro progressive_relaxation(p) -%}
<mark name="stage_prog_relax"/>
{#- VAK TRI-WEAVE: lead with client's primary rep system (NLP 2 p.7-8) -#}
{% set vak_lines = {
  'visual': 'You can see, in the mind\'s eye, a soft light of calm resting at the crown of the head',
  'auditory': 'you can hear how quiet and even the breath is becoming',
  'kinesthetic': 'and you can feel the first wave of softening begin'
} %}
{% set vak_order = {'visual': ['visual','auditory','kinesthetic'], 'auditory': ['auditory','kinesthetic','visual'], 'kinesthetic': ['kinesthetic','visual','auditory']}.get(p.vak, ['visual','auditory','kinesthetic']) %}
{#- PACE current experience → LEAD to relaxation -#}
<p>Rest back now, feeling the rhythm of your breath, giving yourself permission to let me guide you. {{ brk('900ms') }}
